Training source

The full training table and its source snapshot are not redistributed.
The pinned source is Srijit Seal's DILI_Goldstandard_1111.csv at commit
98b7a1b7fba4547cefe936b9890b44baab10e490 in https://github.com/srijitseal/DILI.
That repository carries an MIT software licence, copyright 2024 Srijit Seal.
Its software licence does not establish every underlying clinical-data term.
Users explicitly fetch the table and must respect the original sources' terms.

Validation labels and structures

data/validation contains factual FDA DILIrank 2.0 drug classifications and
PubChem-resolved molecular structures, together with corresponding source
assertions. FDA and NCBI US government-authored information is public domain;
third-party rights and attribution in source records remain applicable.
This package does not claim ownership of source assertions or confer rights
to third-party material. FDA and PubChem do not endorse this model.

Sources:
https://www.fda.gov/science-research/liver-toxicity-knowledge-base-ltkb/drug-induced-liver-injury-rank-dilirank-20-dataset
https://www.fda.gov/about-fda/about-website/website-policies
https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/home/about/policies/

Example fixture

data/example/human_dili_example.parquet contains synthetic molecular structures
and labels, solely for offline harness tests. It contains no clinical training
records and is distributed under the package's Apache-2.0 licence.
